## Concrete renderer plan for a later authorized author continuation

1. Use the existing deterministic JSXGraph-to-SVG route, with instructional display purpose. No artwork/model generation is needed. This is a renderer choice only, not an instantiated spec.
2. Keep two independent panels per figure. Proposed stable prefixes: `fig26-a`, `fig26-b`, `fig27-a`, `fig27-b`; each owns its frame, grid, axes, labels, boundaries, and hatch region.
3. Retain 18-column / 12-row, half-unit, zero-phase lattice structure. Each source-grid inventory group must require a `gridDimensions` assertion mapping to its own finite grid. Do not replace hatch-obscured source grid structure with a blank panel or a unit-only grid.
4. Give observed boundary/grid junctions explicit construction-point IDs. Future collinearity, displacement, and point-on-line assertions must map only points in the owning panel's inventory group. Frame clips remain clips, not visible endpoint markers.
5. Fig. 26a: one straight boundary and one upper-left clipped hatch region. Do not lock exact quarter-unit frame endpoints or restore an unreadable x = 1 label now.
6. Fig. 26b: one steep straight boundary and one right/southeast clipped hatch region. Bind the half-unit x-axis crossing and crowded negative-y crossing separately, preserving their different observational certainty.
7. Fig. 27a: a deterministic circle and two internal vertical segments, with two separate cap hatch regions. Later use point-on-circle and point-on-line assertions for each cap junction after the edition/source interpretation is settled. Do not derive intersection numbers from a solution file.
8. Fig. 27b: two complete straight lines with the same junction; retain all four visible continuations. Use two boundary objects plus one left-wedge hatch region, not a triangular replacement hiding the right-hand lines.
9. Keep hatch strokes distinct from mathematical boundaries and grid strokes. Resolve style uncertainty before selecting full-boundary dash values; scan-induced gaps must not become intentional dashes by accident.
10. Translate source subpanel captions to edition-approved English labels only after exact edition context arrives. Do not add numerical ticks, coordinates, equations, point names, or modern regularization as purported source facts.
11. Measure real exercise-media widths later and use the existing renderer's label/overlap checks at all declared widths, minimum text 16 px. No display width, arrangement change, or render acceptance is asserted in this checkpoint.

